#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "Building an implementation"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "How to turn the blueprint into a running platform on a stack of your choice. The steps are the same for a person and for an agent. Each step ends on a completion criterion; move on only when it holds."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "1. Choose the stack and write the binding"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "Copy the reference binding closest to your stack from [`implementations/`]{1}, or start from [`schema/binding.schema.json`]{2}. For each capability, name the components and their SPDX licences. For each clause, set a status:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "`planned`: you intend to meet it; say `how` if it is not obvious."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "`deviation`: you will not meet it; write the `consequence` and the control that stands in for it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "`not-applicable`: its precondition does not hold; write why."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "**Done when** `just binding <your-binding.yaml>` reports no problems and every deviation names a compensating control."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "2. Lay out the repositories"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "Create one repository per layer, following [CAP-REPOSITORIES]{1}: bootstrap, platform, modules, and one per product. Each has a pinned toolchain and a task runner, and its CI definitions only call tasks. If the repositories will live on more than one CI host, put each host's CI definition beside the others now."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "**Done when** each repository's check task passes on a clean clone, on a workstation and in CI."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "3. Build in dependency order"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "Build capabilities in the order below, which is generated from the dependencies in the catalogue. A capability can be built once everything it depends on is built. Work within the bootstrap layer comes first because every later apply needs its state store and identities."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "For each capability:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "Build it through the CI pipeline, never by hand ([P1]{1})."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "Run each clause's verification as written in its contract."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "Record the evidence (a test, a query and its output, a CI run) in the binding and change the clause's status to `met`."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/building.md
msgid "**Done when** every `MUST` clause of the capability is `met`, or is a recorded deviation."
msgstr ""

